<!-- MC-PATCH: mc-back-button -->
<!-- Lesson 502: chat-UI button as fallback to bridge pill (Lesson 491).
     The bridge pill uses Tauri IPC; this button uses window.location.href
     so it works even if Tauri invoke fails silently on the cross-origin
     page. Both render the same visual style; click handlers are
     independent. Patch is idempotent: this marker prevents re-applying. -->
<script type="module" src="./mc-back-button.js"></script>
<!-- Lesson 243 (rc53.9), Lesson 244 (rc53.10): 🔑 Secrets + 📎 Attach
     floating toolbar at the top-right of the OpenClaw chat page.
     David asked 2026-08-23 for the secrets and dragndrop icons on the
     right side of the chat topbar (which we can't splice into because
     it's a vendored React bundle). Same floating-div pattern as
     mc-back-button.js (Lesson 511 — IPC-INDEPENDENT placement).
     Click handler: rc53.10 prefers the Tauri IPC bridge via
     `window.__openclawHostBridge.invoke('mc_open_overlay', { overlayKey })`,
     which calls the Rust `mc_open_overlay` command. That command
     navigates the main webview to the bundled dashboard URL with
     `#mcAutoOpen=<key>` appended; main.js boot (URL hash → navigate to
     terminal with extras) and terminal.js mount (open overlay + strip
     hash) consume it. URL hash fallback retained for dev/test runs
     without the bridge. mc-chat-toolbar.js has its own idempotent gate. -->
<script type="module" src="./mc-chat-toolbar.js"></script>
